[h1]Portal[/h1]
Portal is a free, unofficial Windows app that turns any real town on OpenStreetMap into a Project Zomboid Build 42 map mod. You search for a place, pick a size and press Generate & Play. A few minutes later the town is installed, with real streets, real street names and furnished buildings.

Download and source: [url=https://github.com/derpasaurus69-crypto/zomboidmods/releases]https://github.com/derpasaurus69-crypto/zomboidmods/releases[/url]

Portal is a front end for [url=https://github.com/spytheeuclidean-a11y/knoxmap]KnoxMap[/url] by euclid80tr, which does the real work of turning map data into a compiled PZ map. KnoxMap is built on Knoxify by arytek. Portal does not include KnoxMap; you install it separately, once.

[h2]What this mod adds[/h2]
This is a small companion mod for towns made with Portal. It is optional. Every Portal town works without it.

With it enabled:
[list]
[*]A [b]Portal[/b] button on the main menu. It lists the Portal towns you have installed, with each town's poster, its size and whether it is enabled.
[*]A short guide to making your own town, with buttons that open this page (which links the download) and copy the download link.
[*]Credits for the projects Portal is built on.
[/list]

It needs no other mod and it does not change the game world.

[h2]Make your own town[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Put Project Zomboid on [b]Build 42[/b] (Properties > Betas on Steam).
[*]Install KnoxMap from [url=https://github.com/spytheeuclidean-a11y/knoxmap]its GitHub page[/url] and run its Setup.bat. You only do this once.
[*]Download Portal.exe from [url=https://github.com/derpasaurus69-crypto/zomboidmods/releases]the releases page[/url] and run it. It opens in your browser.
[*]Search for a town, pick a size and press [b]Generate & Play[/b]. A small area takes a few minutes; a whole town takes 10 to 16 minutes on the developer's PC.
[*]In the game, enable the town under [b]Mods[/b], start a [b]New Game[/b] and pick the town as your spawn region.
[/olist]
A map can only be added to a new world. It will not show up in a save you already have. How good a town looks depends on how well the place is mapped in OpenStreetMap.

[h2]Towns made with Portal[/h2]
All of them are in the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3833268857]Portal collection[/url].
[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3833252919]Bardstown, Kentucky (Town)[/url]

Enable only one Portal town at a time. They all sit at the same spot in the world, so two at once would overlap.

[h2]Status[/h2]
Early release. Tested in singleplayer on one Windows PC. Multiplayer has not been tested. Please report anything that breaks in the comments.

[h2]Real places[/h2]
Portal builds real towns. Streets, place names and public buildings come from OpenStreetMap, which anyone can view. Building interiors, residents and zombies are invented by the generator and do not describe the real places or anyone connected with them.

